11
00:46:05,714 --> 00:46:11,714
Twixt is a 2011 American horror film written, directed,
and produced by Francis Ford Coppola.

12
00:50:17,142 --> 00:50:23,142
It stars Val Kilmer, Bruce Dern, Elle Fanning, Ben Chaplin, Alden
Ehrenreich, David Paymer, Joanne Whalley and Tom Waits.

13
00:54:28,571 --> 00:54:34,571
The film follows a struggling novelist (Kilmer) who stumbles upon a murder mystery in
a small town, in the process entering an alternative, dream world.

14
00:58:40,000 --> 00:58:46,000
The film's title refers to the two worlds explored in the
film, the dream and the waking worlds.

15
01:02:51,428 --> 01:02:57,428
The film premiered on September 4, 2011 at the Toronto International Film Festival and was screened at various film
festivals in North America, receiving a limited theatrical release in a handful of international markets.

16
01:07:02,857 --> 01:07:08,857
It was not well-received by critics, though several reviews were positive, and
Cahiers du cinéma placed it as the third best film of 2012.

17
01:11:14,285 --> 01:11:20,285
Twixt was released on Blu-ray and DVD by Fox Home
Entertainment on July 23, 2013.

18
01:15:25,714 --> 01:15:31,714
A re-edited director's cut, B'Twixt Now and Sunrise, was released theatrically on
September 30, 2022, and on Blu-ray and digital on February 28, 2023.

19
01:19:37,142 --> 01:19:43,142
The film explores themes of sheriff, vampire, orphanage, writer, ghost.

20
